use Libraries.Web.Page.QuorumPage

/*
    Placing Objects.
    Converted from the old Lesson page by plan 13's generator: the same
    words, now without Tailwind.
*/
class PlaceObjects is QuorumPage

    on create
        SetLocation("lessons/Scenes/objects.html")
        // The name lists and links use, and the series and track it belongs
        // to: its section and picture.
        SetShortTitle("Placing Objects")
        SetSectionName("Experience Programming in Quorum (EPIQ)")
        // For search engines and link previews, and what lists of pages say.
        SetDescription("Learn to Placing Objects with the Quorum programming language.")
        SetSummary(" placing objects.")
    end

    action Setup
        SetWebPageTitle("Placing Objects - Quorum Programming Language")
        Title("Placing Objects")
        Paragraph("Learn to place, hide, and use the force on items")
        LearningObjectives()
        PlaceItemsInTheScene10Minutes()
        HideTheItems20Minutes()
        ApplyPhysicsToCharacterMovement20Minutes()
        WrapUp10Minutes()
    end

    private action LearningObjectives
        Section("Learning Objectives")
        Paragraph("We should now have some basic character movement, maps, and other attributes of our game setup. For the next few lessons, our goal is to get a quest up and running. Notably, our goals are to 1) place items that we will use in a quest, and then to 2) get those items in code and tell our running scene to hide them. The reason we are doing this is because we are going to later have our NPC make them magically appear on the screen for our character to go get them.")
        Paragraph("You will:")
        BulletList()
        ListItem("Learn how to hide items in a game")
        ListItem("Learn about Vectors")
        ListItem("Learn to use the force")
    end

    private action PlaceItemsInTheScene10Minutes
        Section("Place Items in the Scene (10 minutes)")
        Paragraph("In our quest, we want our NPC to go have to collect items. Decide what items you want displayed on the screen and place no more than 5-10 of them on your map. Each one should be given a unique name in the property field. We recommend giving them names with a logical incremental ending, like Blue potion 1 and Blue potion 2. This is because in later lessons we will use this property to our advantage.")
    end

    private action HideTheItems20Minutes
        Section("Hide the Items (20 minutes)")
        Paragraph("Now that we have items in the scene, we want them to disappear. The idea is that our NPC is telling us to go find something that they need, which we expose to the player. However, if we load our game right now, these items will show up right away in our game, so we need to hide them. To do this, we 1) in our CreateGame action, find each item like we did before with our character, then 2) for each item, find an action related to showing or hiding the item and call this property. Finding what action to call is an important part of computer science, so practicing looking through documentation can be a helpful way to practice our skills.")
    end

    private action ApplyPhysicsToCharacterMovement20Minutes
        Section("Apply Physics to Character Movement (20 minutes)")
        Paragraph("Now that we have items in our scene and they are hidden, let us go back to our character to clean up the way our character moves. Notably, let's get our character to use physics to move up and down. To do this, we need to learn about the concept of vectors from math and to send vectors to our character's physics system. This will automatically make our character move in a way that adjusts to our map. For example, our character will be able to walk on dirt, but not on water. The 2D physics tutorial on "):Link("using the 2D force", "/tutorials/physics/forceandvelocity2D.html"):Text(" or "):Link("using the 3D force", "/tutorials/physics/forceandvelocity3D.html"):Text(" can both defeat sith lords and is helpful for our programming.")
    end

    private action WrapUp10Minutes
        Section("Wrap-up (10 minutes)")
        Paragraph("For discussion in this lesson, attempt an experiment: move your character around the map and bump into things. Notice that 1) if you move, you keep moving forever, and 2) if you hit corners you can sometimes spin out of control. Can your group come up with a strategy, by looking at the actions we can call on our character, to change these behaviors in our game?")
    end
end
